      "latex_caption": "Empirical distributions of the paired endpoint change $\\Delta\\mathcal E=\\mathcal E_{192}(D_{192})-\\mathcal E_{128}(D_{128})$, in $(\\mathrm{mm}/\\mathrm{s})^2$. Blue and dark gray curves use the posterior mean with measured transport $G_t=R_t^\\top R_{t-1}$ and with $G_t=I_3$, respectively. Each empirical cumulative distribution retains all 256 simulation-level changes, including both tails; positive values indicate a larger error at $t=192$ in the same simulation. These are empirical distributions, with no confidence band. The vertical dashed line marks zero change, not a motion event."
