      "latex_caption": "Directional excitation of the known inputs. Let $S_t=\\beta G_tS_{t-1}G_t^\\top+v_tv_t^\\top$, $s_t=\\beta s_{t-1}+1$, and $H_t=S_t/(\\sigma^2s_t)$, with $S_0=0$, $s_0=0$ and the original $\\beta=0.9$. Blue, orange and pink solid curves give the increasingly ordered eigenvalues $\\lambda_1(H_t)$, $\\lambda_2(H_t)$ and $\\lambda_3(H_t)$, evaluated at the 48 action indices $t=4,8,\\ldots,192$. The vertical scale is logarithmic. The input and measured-frame schedules are shared deterministic quantities, so these curves are not Monte Carlo error means and no uncertainty band is drawn."
