      "latex_caption": "Tangent curvature of the normal posterior during sphere motion. For increasingly ordered eigenvalues of the plane parameter $A_t^+$, define $c_{\\min,t}=2[\\lambda_2(A_t^+)-\\lambda_1(A_t^+)]$ and $c_{\\max,t}=2[\\lambda_3(A_t^+)-\\lambda_1(A_t^+)]$. Blue and orange curves give these curvatures with measured transport; dark gray and light gray give the minimum and maximum with $G_t=I_3$. Curves are arithmetic means over 256 Monte Carlo simulations at the 48 action indices $t=4,8,\\ldots,192$; matching bands give pointwise Student 95\\% confidence intervals for the means. These are angular tangent curvatures of the maintained normal posterior, rather than prediction-error or coverage estimates."
